# One CI gate, one file. See `check-ci-gate-registry.lino` for the convention.
#
# Issue #1047: `cargo nextest --partition slice:N/D` splits by test *index*,
# which is uncorrelated with duration. Measured across run 32591020809 -- 2895
# tests, 4704s of work over eight slices -- index order gave a 870s worst slice
# against a 588s ideal, so the critical path waited 282s on one machine while
# the others sat idle. Longest-processing-time-first reaches 588s exactly.
#
# This gate fails when the planned partitions drift back out of balance, which
# is what happens silently as tests are added and the recorded durations go
# stale. A rebalance is a re-recording, not a code change.
ci_gate check_test_partition_balance
  stage rust
  description "Long tests start first: the planned test partitions stay balanced."
  run "rust-script scripts/plan-test-partition.rs --report --of 8"
